{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## rebar-debug Phase 1 — mechanism proven; legitimacy: intended-behavior / approved superseding design\n\nNo production defect in the existing chain mechanism was found. The observed downgrade is the exact behavior deliberately specified by the original fallback feature, while the requested per-attempt behavior is a later, operator-approved redesign. No Phase 2 bug repair is unlocked by this classification.\n\n### Confirmed mechanism\n\n1. **No fallback currently runs.** The live `rebar.toml` has no `fallback` entry, and the real config lookup returns `fallback_targets_for(\"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\", repo_root=\".\") == ()`. This is the immediate reason the approved direct arm is not exercised.\n2. **Configuring the arm alone deterministically selects PromptedOutput before any attempt.** With the proposed standard slot supplied through the real class parser, runtime values were: candidates `[bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6, anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6]`; per-candidate native flags `[(True, True), (False, False)]`; `_intersect_capabilities` produced `(False, False)`; `structured.output_mode` returned `PromptedOutput` both with and without thinking. The executing path is `runner.py:427-433` -> `_intersect_capabilities` (`runner.py:727-753`) -> `_pai_structured` / `output_mode` (`structured_run.py:186-215`, `structured.py:219+`).\n3. **That up-front collapse is intentional, not an implementation accident.** Original task `worthless-titanite-bubblefish` explicitly decided that capabilities are a conservative intersection computed before the wrapper and requires the whole-chain temperature-withdrawal test. Its tests execute the rule: the restricted candidate withdraws temperature for the entire chain, the all-capable negative control retains it, and capabilities are resolved per candidate rather than from the wrapper (3 focused tests PASS). Story `bixbite-sealbrown-kinkajou` separately requires an all-capable chain to preserve native-under-thinking and a mixed chain to collapse to false; it explicitly records direct Anthropic as unmeasured/fail-closed.\n4. **The wrapper cannot switch output shape per attempt by itself.** A runtime `FallbackModel` probe sent native request parameters to a native-capable primary, forced an availability failure, then reached a prompted-only fallback. The primary entered `request` with `output_mode=native`; the fallback failed in `prepare_request` with `UserError: Native structured output is not supported by this model`. Installed `fallback.py:213-265` accepts one `model_settings` and one `model_request_parameters` object for the whole loop. Therefore simply reading capabilities later does not create per-attempt request shaping; the redesign needs an explicit orchestration seam or candidate adapter.\n5. **The “direct Anthropic is incapable” alternative is now rejected.** A minimal live call using the provisioned non-interactive credential and `NativeOutput` against `anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6` succeeded (`{ok: true}`, finish `stop`). The stronger control with `anthropic_thinking={type: enabled, budget_tokens: 1024}` also succeeded and returned one thinking part. No key value was read or printed. The current false capability is therefore an intentionally fail-closed, not-yet-recorded fact, not current provider inability.\n\n### Legitimacy\n\nClassification: **`intended-behavior`** for the current whole-chain intersection; the requested per-attempt resolution is an **approved superseding design change**, not restoration of the original feature. Authority:\n\n- `worthless-titanite-bubblefish`: whole-chain conservative intersection is a settled decision and AC.\n- `bixbite-sealbrown-kinkajou`: mixed chains must collapse; direct Anthropic remains unmeasured/fail-closed.\n- `disparaged-gratuitous-rooster`: production bot explicitly uses Bedrock with no direct-Anthropic fallback (production scope).\n- This ticket’s later operator decision and the current user direction approve replacing that policy with per-attempt capability resolution and enabling direct Anthropic locally/in CI. That approval supersedes the prior design but does not make the prior implementation a bug.\n\n### Disposition\n\nDo not weaken the existing intersection tests as a bug fix. Treat this ticket as the approved design-change vehicle: specify how a fallback attempt rebuilds output mode, provider-specific cache settings, sampling withdrawals, tools, and provenance when `FallbackModel` exposes only one request shape. The live direct-Anthropic native+thinking result can support a separate measured exact-id capability row, but that alone does not implement the requested general per-attempt policy. No RED contract is supplied because Phase 2 bug repair is not legitimately unlocked."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786298022830870001,"uuid":"be7d9b10-a690-405e-ab13-a1114639d244"}